{
  "version": 1,
  "purpose": "The 37 tile-face glyph assets for the 2.5D rendered view: the 34 standard faces plus the three red fives (akadora). The SVGs are symbol-only and perspective-neutral: they carry no tile body, no shading and no perspective, so the runtime atlas maps one master glyph into every face-up shell's published faceQuad. The blank face has no asset because an empty face is the bare ivory shell.",
  "source": {
    "repo": "https://github.com/SakaiTaka23/riichi-mahjong-tiles",
    "path": "Regular/regular",
    "commit": "f37d6cc2557498d23f13eb3e955e0e44e5c863ff",
    "variant": "regular symbol-only SVG, 300 x 400 viewBox, transparent background",
    "license": "CC0 1.0 public domain (upstream README: 'All assets are in the public domain')",
    "notes": "The upstream Regular-Blank.svg is a red question mark, not an empty tile face, so it is deliberately not vendored. Haku (5z) is a real face: its symbol-only SVG rasterises to zero ink because a white dragon has no printed symbol."
  },
  "raster": {
    "width": 288,
    "height": 384,
    "format": "8-bit RGBA PNG",
    "background": "transparent",
    "shapeRendering": 2,
    "paint": {
      "redBase": "#b93c3c",
      "red": "#a60c0c"
    },
    "rationale": "288 x 384 is 2.4-2.5x the @2x face axes of the Phase 1c base (up to 118 px on the upright/sideways shells and 117 px on the outer hand slots), so the atlas only ever downsamples even at pixelRatio 2. The 300 x 400 upstream canvas is scaled uniformly to 0.96, keeping the symbol's own margins and its pixel-for-pixel alignment with the upstream full-face variant."
  },
  "output": {
    "dir": "../../frontend/public/table/faces",
    "manifest": "../../frontend/public/table/faces.json",
    "bytesBudget": 1310720
  },
  "faces": [
